  "what_this_is": "M5/E12 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-17-node-context-policy-design.md section 16, cell B8b; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-16-slurp-v2-base-program-design.md section 3 item E12; owner directive 26 of 2026-09-18): the four-row form smoke of cell B8b, ONE factor on top of cell B7r's configuration (configs/baseline/slurp-native-anchor-ncp-l1-reviewer-format-smoke-4-v1.json), whose sealed bytes are the primary comparator. The moved key is native_episode.reviewer_audit, the fifth and last member of the episode class's closed allowlist: it arms the deterministic, zero-contact slot-audit context block at the reviewer:current-draft boundary, rendered from the committed construction table knowledge/slurp/semantic/slot-audit-v1 (60 intents, 54 entity types, 9,354 TRAIN construction utterances after the 2026-09-13 exclusion) through the committed template configs/probes/ncp_slurp_slot_audit_reviewer_v1.txt. The block APPENDS the intent's construction slot profile and the four harness-computed flags (TYPE-UNSEEN, EMPTY-DRAFT, MISSING-COMMON, REPRESENTATION) after the L1 draft block, which is itself byte-identical to B7r's. NOTHING ELSE moves against B7r: the same node context policy with the same eight structured boundaries, the same templates and the same on_parse_failure rules, the same Reviewer response format saea-review-findings-v1, the same four tool-observation boundaries at raw, no cleaning contact, the shared four-row engineering roster, the same model fragment and resident geometry, the same promoted EVO-FOLDS-V2 packets, both knowledge stores at v1 with their release/snapshot pins and their supply geometry, the same prepared Perception supply, the same instruction templates and the same scorers. The block makes ZERO contacts of any kind, so the contact ceiling stays 11 and no budget moves. It is authored from construction data only -- no gold of any evaluated row, no filler, no sentence, no utterance id -- and the audit's own saea-reviewer-slot-audit-v1 receipt binds every rendered block to the table pins, the template hash and the flag counts. Fold B is absent. The separate generation and native fit identities do not authorize contact.",
